==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|bindan|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|bʰendʰ-|bind|lang=ang}}.  Cognate with Old High German [[bintan]] (German [[binden]]), Old Norse [[binda]] (Swedish [[binda]]), Middle Low German ''binden'' (Dutch [[binden]]).  The IE root was also the source of Avestan ''bendayaiti'' and Greek {{polytonic|[[πεῖσμα]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/'bindɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
'''bindan'''

# to [[bind]], [[constrain]]
# to [[fasten]] or [[join]]

